# strings1 — SET, GET and quoting
#
# Learn: a string key holds one value. redis-cli splits a line on spaces,
# so a value containing spaces has to be quoted, just like in a shell.
#
# Task: store the user's full name "Ada Lovelace" under user:1:name and
# her language "en" under user:1:lang. Right now the first command is
# rejected with a syntax error.
#

SET user:1:name Ada Lovelace
SET user:1:lang en
GET user:1:name
